course: dictionary
lesson: 15230
title: Shaken: moved or upset
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Shaken has two jobs. First, it is a form of the verb shake: shake, shook, shaken. You use shaken after has, have, had, or was and were: «The jar has been shaken.» Here it means moved quickly up and down or side to side.
explain: Second, shaken can describe a feeling. «After the near miss, Sam was shaken.» It means upset, frightened or shocked after something bad has happened. Check your meaning by swapping in upset or frightened. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Context gives you the clue. A shaken bottle of fizzy drink is being moved, so the drink fizzes over. A shaken person has had a fright. Ask yourself: is something being moved, or is someone feeling something? That tells you which meaning to use.
fact: Shake is a verb. Its forms are shake, shook, shaken and shaking.
fact: As a verb, «shaken» means moved quickly up and down or side to side.
fact: As an adjective, «shaken» means upset, frightened or shocked after something bad has happened.
fact: The phrase «shaken up» means upset or scared after a shock.
fact: Use shook for the past: «Yesterday the wind shook the old tree.» Use shaken after has, have or had: «The old tree has been shaken by the storm.»
exercise: Mia has ___ the bottle well before she opens it. Which word fits? | shaking | *shaken | shake | shook
exercise: «The bottle has been shaken before opening.» What does shaken mean here? | *Moved quickly up and down | Very cold | Hungry and tired | Upset and frightened
exercise: «After the crash, the driver was shaken but unhurt.» What does shaken mean? | *Upset and shocked | Happy to be home | Moved up and down | Very tired and hungry
test: What does shaken mean in «After the scary dream, Ruby was still shaken»? | Moved up and down | Hungry | *Upset and frightened | Very clean
test: Dad has ___ the paint tin for a long time. Which word fits? | shook | shaking | *shaken | shake
exam: Which sentence uses shaken to mean moved up and down? | «He felt shaken after the test.» | «The shaken children hugged their mum.» | «She was shaken by the sad news.» | *«The bottle was shaken, so the drink fizzed over.»
